    {
      "id": 157362,
      "name": "Voob Gooblin",
      "username": "Voob_Gooblin",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/voob_gooblin/{size}/2504_2.png",
      "created_at": "2016-03-16T19:26:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Revisiting, because I played a game where this came up and it felt far too overpowered, so thought of a possible counter-argument:</p><blockquote><p><span>Nothing stops anyone in this game from trying to do something they can't do to no effect.&nbsp;</span></p></blockquote><p>If that is the logic for enabling TtE to change X's damage to Radiant, thereby nullifying damage attempted by X, couldn't you also argue that Visionary via TtE may&nbsp;<i>attempt</i>&nbsp;to change the damage type, but to no effect—because of Radiant's impossibility—allowing the original damage type to be dealt, despite \"using\" TtE for that instance?</p><p>So making an option C) Visionary chooses Radiant damage; the damage type does not change</p>",
      "post_number": 11,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:37:17.446Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
      "reads": 0,
      "readers_count": 0,
      "score": 0.0,
      "yours": false,
      "topic_id": 14278,
      "topic_slug": "targets-cannot-do-radiant-damage",
      "display_username": "Voob Gooblin",
      "primary_group_name": null,
      "flair_name": null,
      "flair_url": null,
      "flair_bg_color": null,
      "flair_color": null,
      "flair_group_id": null,
      "badges_granted": [],
      "version": 1,
      "can_edit": false,
      "can_delete": false,
      "can_recover": false,
      "can_see_hidden_post": false,
      "can_wiki": false,
      "read": false,
      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>Revisiting, because I played a game where this came up and it felt far too overpowered, so thought of a possible counter-argument:</p><blockquote><p><span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51); font-family: 'Open Sans', HelveticaNeue, 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14.4px; line-height: 21.6px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">Nothing stops anyone in this game from trying to do something they can&#39;t do to no effect.&nbsp;</span></p></blockquote><p>If that is the logic for enabling TtE to change X&#39;s damage to Radiant, thereby nullifying damage attempted by X, couldn&#39;t you also argue that Visionary via TtE may&nbsp;<i>attempt</i>&nbsp;to change the damage type, but to no effect&mdash;because of Radiant&#39;s impossibility&mdash;allowing the original damage type to be dealt, despite &quot;using&quot; TtE for that instance?</p><p>So making an option C) Visionary chooses Radiant damage; the damage type does not change</p>",
